<BaseLayout title="Support — EyeOh" description="Help with EyeOh audio and camera switching for macOS.">
  <article class="container legal-copy legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Support</p><h1>Small app. Short answers.</h1>
    <h2>An app did not follow the selected microphone or speaker</h2><p>Teams, Zoom, and similar apps can be pinned to a named device. Choose “Default” or “System” in that app so it follows the macOS route selected by EyeOh.</p>
    <h2>An app did not follow the preferred camera</h2><p>EyeOh sets macOS’s preferred camera, but meeting and browser apps can retain their own selection. Choose the system or automatic camera option when available.</p>
    <h2>Camera preview is unavailable</h2><p>Open System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Camera and allow EyeOh. Preview starts only when requested and stops when its window closes.</p>
    <h2>A device is missing</h2><p>Confirm it appears in System Settings → Sound, reconnect the USB or Bluetooth device, then use Refresh Devices in EyeOh Settings.</p>
    <h2>Get help</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:darkice@darkice.co?subject=EyeOh%20feedback">darkice@darkice.co</a> or use Send Feedback inside EyeOh. Include the device type and what you expected. Please do not send recordings or private meeting information.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
